          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Directed Homotopy Theory is a variant of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            which aims to study the properties of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+spaces"} directed spaces
          %p Much of the impetus for the theory comes from work on modelling concurrent process. It can also be seen as a way of studying an ‘evolving’ space.
          %p The following examples illustrate the sort of problems that arise:
          %h2#example Example
          %p
            The example uses two directed spaces that are slightly different and use a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pospace"} pospace
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                    %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                    %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x,y)\leq (x\prime, y\prime)
            if and only if
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi y
                    %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                      %mo ′
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi x
                    %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                      %mo ′
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |y\prime - y| \leq x\prime - x
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/future+cone"} future cone
            of any point is a cone symmetric about a horizontal line through the point and with edges at
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ±
                  %mn 45
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pm 45
            degrees to that line.)
