                %tspan#tspan4559{"sodipodi:role" => "line", :x => "444.83432", :y => "214.36501"} p'
          %p
            In both the space is the rectangle with two smaller rectangles removed. The position of the upper left small rectangle is the same in both, but that of the righthand lower rectangle is shifted slightly to the right in the second picture. The directed homotopy classes of d-paths from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                      %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^\prime
            in the two cases are different. The crucial point is that in the second there is such a class that was impossible in the first example, yet the spaces are homeomorphic, so classically would be ‘the same’. The subtlety is in the order.
          %h3#problem Problem
          %p
            The first problem is to find a small model of such structures. The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+category"} fundamental category
            would be a model, but unlike with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+groupoid"} fundamental groupoid
            in the non-directed case, it is not sufficient to take a ‘base point’ in each connected component. That would ignore the order.
          %h2#RelatedConcepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+homotopy+type+theory"} directed homotopy type theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/models+for+concurrency"}> models for concurrency
                ;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+data+analysis"} topological data analysis
                and
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/persistent+homology"} persistent homology
            %li
              %p
                Models for mixed temporal-spatial
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+logics"} modal logics
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+sets"}> causal sets
                , discrete models for space time and
                %span.newWikiWord
                  causal models
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/causal+models"} ?
                in Computer Science, Physics and Systems Biology;
            %li
              %p
                models for multi-agent systems,
                %span.newWikiWord
                  multimodal logics
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/multimodal+logics"} ?
          %h2#references References
          %p
            (See also under
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+space"} directed space
          %p
            Foundational work was done by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Goubault"} Eric Goubault
            and his collaborators.
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Goubault"}> Eric Goubault
              ,
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Some+geometric+perspectives+in+concurrency+theory"} Some geometric perspectives in concurrency theory
          %p Categorical aspects are looked at in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lisbeth+Fajstrup"} Lisbeth Fajstrup
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ji%C5%99%C3%AD+Rosick%C3%BD"} Jiří Rosický
              = succeed "," do
                %em A convenient category for directed homotopy
              %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/21/1/21-01abs.html"} online
          %p
            For more on this see also at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Delta-generated+space"} Delta-generated space
          %p Applications to computer science are presented in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lisbeth+Fajstrup"}> Lisbeth Fajstrup
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Goubault"} Eric Goubault
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Emmanuel+Haucourt"} Emmanuel Haucourt
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Samuel+Mimram"} Samuel Mimram
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Raussen"} Martin Raussen
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Directed+Algebraic+Topology+and+Concurrency"} Directed Algebraic Topology and Concurrency
          %p The fundamental category of a pospace is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lisbeth+Fajstrup"}> Lisbeth Fajstrup
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Goubault"} Eric Goubault
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Emmanuel+Haucourt"} Emmanuel Haucourt
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Raussen"} Martin Raussen
          %p and the possibility of an analogue of covering spaces in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lisbeth+Fajstrup"}> Lisbeth Fajstrup
              , Dicovering spaces. Algebraic topological methods in computer science (Stanford, CA, 2001). Homology Homotopy Appl. 5 (2003), no. 2, 1-17
              %p
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.intlpress.com/HHA/v5/n2/"}> HHA
                )
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Philippe+Gaucher"} Philippe Gaucher
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/PPS"}> PPS
            , Paris) has introduced an interesting related model, namely that of ‘flows’. These are, approximately, topological categories without identity arrows. They are intended as another model of processes. One of his papers on this idea is at
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0308054v1"} Arxiv
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Philippe+Gaucher"}> Philippe Gaucher
              , A model category for the homotopy theory of concurrency, Homology Homotopy and Applications, vol. 5 (1):p.549-599, 2003.
          %p
            Marco Grandis’ work on the area is listed amongst his publications at his (
            %a{:href => "http://www.dima.unige.it/~grandis/rec.public_grandis.html"}> homepage
            ). Such as
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marco+Grandis"}> Marco Grandis
                , Directed homotopy theory. I, Cah. Topol. G eom. Di er. Cat eg. 44 (4) (2003) 281–316.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marco+Grandis"}> Marco Grandis
                , Directed homotopy theory. II. Homotopy constructs, Theory Appl. Categ. 10 (2002) No. 14, 369–391 (electronic).
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marco+Grandis"}> Marco Grandis
                , The shape of a category up to directed homotopy, Theory Appl. Categ. 15 (2005/06) No. 4, 95–146 (electronic).
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marco+Grandis"}> Marco Grandis
                , Modelling fundamental 2-categories for directed homotopy, Homology, Homotopy Appl. 8 (1) (2006) 31–70 (electronic)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marco+Grandis"}> Marco Grandis
                ,
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Directed+Algebraic+Topology"}> Directed Algebraic Topology
                  , Models of non-reversible worlds
                , Cambridge University Press, 2009.
          %p A websearch will find others.
          %p Another approach to model category structures in this area is by Kahl, who uses a Baues type fibration category approach.
          %ul
            %li
              Thomas Kahl, Relative directed homotopy theory of partially ordered spaces, Journal of Homotopy and Related Structures, Vol. 1(2006), No. 1, pp. 79-100,(
              %a{:href => "http://jhrs.rmi.acnet.ge/volumes/2006/n1a4/"}> JHRS
              ).
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Krzysztof+Worytkiewicz"} Krzysztof Worytkiewicz
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Bubenik"} Peter Bubenik
            have given a model category structure for local pospaces:
          %ul
            %li
              P. Bubenik and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K.+Worytkiewicz"} K. Worytkiewicz
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "http://intlpress.com/HHA/v8/n1/a10/"} HHA
          %p Further related references are
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L.+Fajstrup"}> L. Fajstrup
                , Loops, ditopology and deadlocks, Math. Structures Comput. Sci. 10 (4) (2000) 459–480, geometry and concurrency.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L.+Fajstrup"}> L. Fajstrup
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M.+Raussen"} M. Raussen
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E.+Goubault"} E. Goubault
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E.+Haucourt"} E. Haucourt
              %p theory.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L.+Fajstrup"}> L. Fajstrup
                , Dihomotopy classes of dipaths in the geometric realization of a cubical set: from discrete to continuous and back again, in: R. Kopperman, M. B. Smyth, D. Spreen, J. Webster (Eds.),
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Spatial Representation: Discrete vs. Continuous Computational Models
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L.+Fajstrup"}> L. Fajstrup
                , Dipaths and dihomotopies in a cubical complex, Adv. in Appl.
              %p Math. 35 (2) (2005) 188–206.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M.+Raussen"}> M. Raussen
                , Deadlocks and dihomotopy in mutual exclusion models, in: R. Kopperman, M. B. Smyth, D. Spreen, J. Webster (Eds.),
                %em Spatial
              %p Representation: Discrete vs. Continuous Computational Models, no. 04351 in Dagstuhl Seminar Proceedings_, IBFI, Schloss Dagstuhl, Germany, 2005.
            %li
              %p
                U. Fahrenberg,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M.+Raussen"} M. Raussen
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.aau.dk/research/reports/2006.htm"} preprint R-2006-22
                (2006).
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E.+Goubault"}> E. Goubault
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E.+Haucourt"} E. Haucourt
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://iml.univ-mrs.fr/lafont/Geocal/goubault2.pdf"} web
              %p (2006).23
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E.+Goubault"}> E. Goubault
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Emmanuel+Haucourt"} E. Haucourt
              %p technical reports, CEA, Saclay (2006).
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M.+Raussen"}> M. Raussen
                , Invariants of directed spaces, available as preprint R-2006-28 (
                %a{:href => "http://bib.mathematics.dk/preprint.php?id=DMF-2006-08-002"}> web
                )(2006).
